        "original_id": "01c7e04c-a090-5ca2-adf9-c1c6cde16497",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Aneesh Lee Ashok, Binu S, Deepak Dev, Shine Tom Chacko\n- Films: Ithihasa, Ee Adutha Kaalathu, Chapters, Annayum Rasoolum, Masala Republic, Chronic Bachelor, Udayananu Tharam, Naran, Puthiya Mukham, Urumi, Grandmaster, Bhaskar the Rascal\n- Topics: Malayalam cinema, body-swapping\n\nFacts:\n- Deepak Devraj Komath, known as Deepak Dev, is an Indian music composer best known for his work in Malayalam cinema.\n- Deepak Dev is known for compositions in films including \"Chronic Bachelor,\" \"Udayananu Tharam,\" \"Naran,\" \"Puthiya Mukham,\" \"Urumi,\" \"Grandmaster,\" and \"Bhaskar the Rascal.\"\n- In 2014, \"Ithihasa\" was released as a Malayalam fantasy comedy film written by Aneesh Lee Ashok and directed by Binu S.\n- In 2014, Shine Tom Chacko played his first lead role in Binu S Kalady's fantasy-comedy film \"Ithihasa.\"\n- \"Ithihasa\" deals with body-swapping.\n- Before his first lead role, Shine Tom Chacko played supporting roles in \"Ee Adutha Kaalathu,\" \"Chapters,\" \"Annayum Rasoolum,\" and \"Masala Republic.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
